@startuml v1-daemon
title Companion to M-DP1: v1 daemon; SH2+ backend disabled until activation gate
participant "Caller process\ncaller UID / principal + key" as C
participant "swarma-dispatcher daemon\nservice UID swarma-dispatcher\nowns admission, input/agent/run records, claims, cleanup" as D
participant "swarma-session-host\nSH2+ own service UID\nowns metadata, logs, receipts, fences, input admission" as SH
participant "swarma-user-launcher\nroot until agent UID drop; receipt writer" as L
participant "swarma-session-runner\nSH2+ agent UID\nowns PTY/app-server and renewal" as SR
participant "Credential broker\nunprivileged; owns binding / grant / lease state" as B
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; owns account ledger / stop evidence" as H
C -> D : connect; peer UID; server identity; hello; signed dispatch
alt authentication / permission / version / malformed response failure
  break transport refusal
    D --> C : failure; client never falls back to v0
  end
else ambiguous reply
  C -> D : repeat same request_id and signature
end
D -> D : reconcile; prepare authority, quota, capacity
alt quota / authority failure
  break permanent refusal
    D --> C : typed refusal; never queue
  end
else temporary capacity closure
  D -> D : persist bounded fair queue
  D --> C : queued handle
  ... gate opens ...
  D -> D : recheck principal, authority/window, quotas and all gates
  alt authority / quota / window refuses at dequeue
    break no launch
      D --> C : typed refusal
    end
  else capacity remains closed
    break remain queued
      D -> D : retain durable queue; no launch
    end
  end
end
== admitted request only ==
D -> D : provision; owned execution claim; journal distinct effects
alt SH2+ backend gates published and activated (§§12, 14)
  D -> SH : start {logical_session_id, execution_id, controller_epoch, op_id, ticket}
  alt fence / current controller epoch invalid
    SH --> D : refuse effect; live pid is not controller authority
  else fence + epoch validated atomically with effect
    SH -> L : host-role launch.start + dispatcher ticket
    alt wrong host principal, reused ticket, wrong generation/executor/plan, revoked claim
      L --> SH : refuse launch
    else valid unused ticket for dispatcher-owned generation
      L -> L : user-manager shared lock + journal: redeem once for authenticated host
      L -> L : write start receipt while root
      L -> SR : reset; clear groups; set GID/UID; exec
      SR -> B : own broker connection; qualified lease and renewal
      SH --> D : receipts/events
    end
  end
  note over D,SR
    Ticket signature/version/canonical bytes and host-role schema
    are unspecified in spec §§12, 16; backend remains disabled.
    Dispatcher only issues ticket; host presents it; user-manager launcher redeems.
    Ownership handoffs must be specified before activation.
    Standing-session execution runtime is open: R3 proposal in §16; §3.5 unchanged.
    SH1 behavior is unspecified in spec §12; no SH1 migration is asserted.
    Log handoff is unspecified in spec §16 (open question 5).
  end note
else default supervisor backend
  D -> D : service-UID supervision -> root launcher -> agent-UID curator-run\n(§5.3 intake / Decision 0021 / qualification gate)
end
opt stop / cancel / recovery for an execution that launched
  D -> H : exec.stop (journaled E-stop; own generation/execution)
  alt termination observation unknown / contradictory
    D -> D : retain state + capacity; same-effect retry; never relaunch
  else termination confirmed
    H --> D : no execution process remains
    D -> D : record outcome; applicable cleanup; terminal after confirmation
  end
end
D --> C : events / current execution record; outcome separate from state
note over D
  Internal sweep never expires standing allocations; no lifetime quota.
  Standing retirement/re-creation is operator-only with signed record (§5.4).
  Distinct downstream effect IDs, retries reuse IDs.
  v0 -> v1: stop admission, exclusive state, check/migrate, drain v0 supervisors,
  reconcile, switch recorded mode, ready. Rollback reverses the steps (§11).
  Board/host clients never embed broker clients (§5.3).
  Exact event payloads and recovery delivery are unspecified in spec §§8, 12, 14.
  Broker service UID spelling is unspecified in spec §3.1.
end note
legend
  Defining spec: [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#83-v1-socket-dispatch1 §8.3 socket]]
  [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#12-session-host-backend-later-activation-gate §12 backend]] / §§7, 9, 11, 14
endlegend
@enduml
